Z||000015||Sage||11-18-2001||11:05 AM||||Must have seen 30 - 40 in an hour and a half period from about 4:15 to 5:45 A.M..  Was great!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Kind of another reminder that we are just one of the hunks of dirt hanging in space, and that there are too many others to count.<P><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||14
Z||000016||fierohoho||11-18-2001||11:39 AM||||Set the alarm for 4:00am, got up and kicked the wife out of bed, we made some hot coco and took a blanket out to the pasture. <P>We were seeing about 10-20 per minute. It was perfectly clear. <P>Stayed out till about 5:30am. <P>Haven't seen a shower that good before.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||btoth||11-18-2001||11:54 AM||||I just happened to wake up at around 5:30.  So I stared out my windows for about 15 minutes and saw maybe 10 really fast streaks in the sky.  Pretty cool.  The one that I thought was cool was a slow (well, slow compaired to the others) moving really big bright dot (looked just like the other stars in the sky), falling downwards at an angle... no tail behind it until right before it disapeared.  Must have been a big one.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
