Z||000023||Ken Wittlief||11-19-2001||12:41 AM||||That was kinda neat  - around 5AM was seeing on every few seconds, sometimes 2 or 3 at once.<P> and there were a few that went half way across the sky, glowed reddish and yellow, and left a green trail in the sky.<P> one trail lasted about 8 seconds, it hung there glowing green.<P> It was interesting for about a half hour - but I wouldnt say it was spectacular or anything - not like Ive never seen a meaty oar before.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Gerald||11-19-2001||01:08 AM||||The DD puled the van over so us drunks could stumble out to the side o the road and watch. Not a cloud in the sky and I was drunk enuf that the cold didnt brother me. I wont for get that night for a very long time. I watched for 15 mins on the side of the road and another 30 at my friends house.||||reg||1
